      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>We are dedicated to preventing the dhole (cuon alpinus) from going extinct. We do this by providing funding for research on the ground conservation efforts while also providing free education and awareness programs.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Expanded effrots in Nepal to allow for more community outreach. Efforts from 2024 showed that Nepal most likely has a robust dhole population, more ecological surveys are needed to confirm this. Parters with IUCN agree that outreach and community involvement is the largest hurdles for dhole populations in the country. Partnered with NCSC to do more community outreach in the Nepal region.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>600</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ForeignGrantsInd>X</ForeignGrantsInd>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>600</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Support for a new Ph.D project in Thailand, a better understanding of the dhole range in the country. looking at pack range, resource use, and land use of dhole packs in the northern range of the country.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>1002</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ForeignGrantsInd>X</ForeignGrantsInd>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>1002</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Started an ecology project in Cambodia in the Cardamom Mountains. This area is between two national parks Botum Sakor National Park and Southern Cardamoms Nationa Park. This has been seen to be a wildlife highway. Dholes are known to be in the area, but their abundance and ecology are not well understood in the area. No financial support was given in 2024, but time and expertise were given.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>0</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Contuinuted World Dhole Day events. Focused on those in dhole range countries like Nepal and Cambodia. Also included more online activities and classroom lesson plans. This included the implementation of a volunteer committee to expand education and awareness efforts.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>500</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ForeignGrantsInd>X</ForeignGrantsInd>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>500</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
